es: 1. Rookery upstream or double-count. 2. Instrument issue. Investigate, report findings.\"\n    },\n    \"Wickett\": {\n      \"register\": \"wry\",\n      \"engine\": \"ollama:llama3.2:latest\",\n      \"stub\": false,\n      \"text\": \"The thrill of possibly having a rookery upstream and a duckweed problem with the turbidity probe. Well, let's get down to business. It seems like we have some... interesting data points to review. I'll start by reviewing the station 4 heron count - tripled, you say? That's a 300% increase. Not exactly a statistically significant anomaly, but I suppose it's worth looking into. The question is, what's the probability of a new rookery suddenly appearing upstream, and what are the implications for our understanding of local migration patterns?\"\n    }\n  },"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"2d174e","exit_code":0,"signal":null}}}}}
