{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#24a0d50edb7649f7ad7aa0a3b255b01b","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"| C-ReadinessGate | conform | `app/gate.py` — real checks (component registry, pipeline route probe, LLM handle, durabl\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n+queryable+mounted ledger); pass time recorded in 4 places; time-to-gate metric in evidence |\n| C-LaunchPartition | conform | `runtime/launch-partition.jsonl` — real dedicated launch file, dependency-ordered mount\u001b[0m,\u001b[0m\n id-deduped vs journal |\n| C-TransientBoundary | conform | `runtime/transient/` + boot marker; dirty shutdown resets the boundary only |\n| C-SnapshotInference | conform | `ledger.snapshot()` `SnapshotView`; parallel respondent draft threads each read their\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nown snapshot; `inference:snapshot` rows |\n| C-SequentialCommit | conform | verified drafts commit in ranked order via `persona.speak`; `inference:commit` rows re\u001b[0mc\u001b[0m\nord sequence + reactsTo |\n\n## Convention conformance / recorded challenges (direction-002)\n\nConventions are challengeable, never ignorable. Recorded challenges for the\nv0.1-only set (F4) and related conventions:\n\n| Convention | Conform / challenge | Record |\n|---|---|---|\n| C-JsonlLedger, C-LocalIndices, C-DyadicConfidence, C-CertaintyPrivilege, C-UnmetNeedRecords, C-AcceptanceChecks, C-Mu\u001b[0ml\u001b[0m\ntiSourceAccess, C-CompetingSources, C-SpecializedListRetrieval, C-ConfiguredAccounts, C-ConvergentOntology | conform | \u001b[0mc\u001b[0m\narried from baseline; unchanged semantics |\n| C-EthicsGate | **conform+** | gate now does liveness research via the live wikipedia connector + maxim:objection refu\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\nals + cards; imitation mark is a floor, not the whole gate |\n| C-PresentationGlass | conform | persona art asset pipeline: seeded composition, portrait frames, ambient SVG motion, \u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\nrtifacts + `persona:art` rows, re-render supersedes |\n| C-ConversationArchive | conform | `archive-view` computed segments + per-turn rows + `archive:segment` sealing |\n| C-SetBuild | conform | `setbuild.py` — competing retrievals, criteria on the need, non-match classes retained, closur\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n + artifact |\n| C-AgenticProtocol | conform | need→gate→invoke→outcome/churn protocol is the tool lifecycle; `compare-run` generalize\u001b[0ms\u001b[0m\n competition over it |\n| C-ConnectorSet | **challenge (recorded)** | convention describes a 17-connector catalog; owner direction-002 scopes t\u001b[0mh\u001b[0m\nis cycle to 3 real runnable connectors — 4 delivered (wikipedia, ics-calendar, files, rss), all end-to-end. Evaluation:\u001b[0m \u001b[0m\nmachinery is general (`CONNECTORS` registry + configured-source assertions); breadth beyond the delivered set is connec\u001b[0mt\u001b[0m\nor-authoring, not new machinery |\n| C-PerceivableRespondents, C-SequentialRespondents, C-SpeechFloor | conform | floor serializes playback; sequence indi\u001b[0mc\u001b[0m\nes on cards + `decision:respondent` rows |\n| C-PersonalityArt, C-VoiceDiversity | conform | `art.py` unique art; rotated real SAPI voices + `persona:voice` modifi\u001b[0ma\u001b[0m\nble assertions |\n| C-ScenarioEnactment, C-CanonicalScenarios | conform | `evidence/scenarios/*.json` are live-run transcripts, not sourc\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\n inspection |\n| C-DeclaredStubs, C-HonestyBanner | conform | banner + `launch:honesty` rows; remote TTS/OAuth connectors declared unc\u001b[0mo\u001b[0m\nnfigured |\n| C-DesktopShell / C-FullScreen / ranked-OS | **partial conform / challenge (recorded)** | `launch.cmd` + `python -m ap\u001b[0mp\u001b[0m\n --open` launches like an installed program on Windows; window-close terminates the program via SSE watchdog (S-close-t\u001b[0me\u001b[0m\nrminate enacted). Still a browser surface, not a native shell — direction did not scope one |\n\n## Honesty notes\n\n- `llm` engine: `live-ollama` when reachable (model picked from `/api/tags`,\n  preferring text models), otherwise `stub` — the fallback reply text itself\n  declares `[declared stub]`; the banner always shows the mode.\n- `render-speech-remote` is registered and competes, but honestly reports\n  `unconfigured` until a source grant exists — it never substitutes silently.\n- `mail.outbox_write` writes `.eml` artifacts to `runtime/outbox/` — it claims\n  local queueing, never network delivery.\n- Host-backed `fn` tools are marked `hasFn` in the component manifest (a\n  declared divergence from the reference's all-data posture for\n  orchestrators); user-authored tools are data-only and validated."}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","cognition.ai/terminalPreview":true}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","toolCallId":"exec:0#24a0d50edb7649f7ad7aa0a3b255b01b","status":"in_progress","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"| C-ReadinessGate | conform | `app/gate.py` — real checks (component registry, pipeline route probe, LLM handle, durable+queryable+mounted ledger); pass time recorded in 4 places; time-to-gate metric in evidence |\n| C-LaunchPartition | conform | `runtime/launch-partition.jsonl` — real dedicated launch file, dependency-ordered mount, id-deduped vs journal |\n| C-TransientBoundary | conform | `runtime/transient/` + boot marker; dirty shutdown resets the boundary only |\n| C-SnapshotInference | conform | `ledger.snapshot()` `SnapshotView`; parallel respondent draft threads each read their own snapshot; `inference:snapshot` rows |\n| C-SequentialCommit | conform | verified drafts commit in ranked order via `persona.speak`; `inference:commit` rows record sequence + reactsTo |\n\n## Convention conformance / recorded challenges (direction-002)\n\nConventions are challengeable, never ignorable. Recorded challenges for the\nv0.1-only set (F4) and related conventions:\n\n| Convention | Conform / challenge | Record |\n|---|---|---|\n| C-JsonlLedger, C-LocalIndices, C-DyadicConfidence, C-CertaintyPrivilege, C-UnmetNeedRecords, C-AcceptanceChecks, C-MultiSourceAccess, C-CompetingSources, C-SpecializedListRetrieval, C-ConfiguredAccounts, C-ConvergentOntology | conform | carried from baseline; unchanged semantics |\n| C-EthicsGate | **conform+** | gate now does liveness research via the live wikipedia connector + maxim:objection refusals + cards; imitation mark is a floor, not the whole gate |\n| C-PresentationGlass | conform | persona art asset pipeline: seeded composition, portrait frames, ambient SVG motion, artifacts + `persona:art` rows, re-render supersedes |\n| C-ConversationArchive | conform | `archive-view` computed segments + per-turn rows + `archive:segment` sealing |\n| C-SetBuild | conform | `setbuild.py` — competing retrievals, criteria on the need, non-match classes retained, closure + artifact |\n| C-AgenticProtocol | conform | need→gate→invoke→outcome/churn protocol is the tool lifecycle; `compare-run` generalizes competition over it |\n| C-ConnectorSet | **challenge (recorded)** | convention describes a 17-connector catalog; owner direction-002 scopes this cycle to 3 real runnable connectors — 4 delivered (wikipedia, ics-calendar, files, rss), all end-to-end. Evaluation: machinery is general (`CONNECTORS` registry + configured-source assertions); breadth beyond the delivered set is connector-authoring, not new machinery |\n| C-PerceivableRespondents, C-SequentialRespondents, C-SpeechFloor | conform | floor serializes playback; sequence indices on cards + `decision:respondent` rows |\n| C-PersonalityArt, C-VoiceDiversity | conform | `art.py` unique art; rotated real SAPI voices + `persona:voice` modifiable assertions |\n| C-ScenarioEnactment, C-CanonicalScenarios | conform | `evidence/scenarios/*.json` are live-run transcripts, not source inspection |\n| C-DeclaredStubs, C-HonestyBanner | conform | banner + `launch:honesty` rows; remote TTS/OAuth connectors declared unconfigured |\n| C-DesktopShell / C-FullScreen / ranked-OS | **partial conform / challenge (recorded)** | `launch.cmd` + `python -m app --open` launches like an installed program on Windows; window-close terminates the program via SSE watchdog (S-close-terminate enacted). Still a browser surface, not a native shell — direction did not scope one |\n\n## Honesty notes\n\n- `llm` engine: `live-ollama` when reachable (model picked from `/api/tags`,\n  preferring text models), otherwise `stub` — the fallback reply text itself\n  declares `[declared stub]`; the banner always shows the mode.\n- `render-speech-remote` is registered and competes, but honestly reports\n  `unconfigured` until a source grant exists — it never substitutes silently.\n- `mail.outbox_write` writes `.eml` artifacts to `runtime/outbox/` — it claims\n  local queueing, never network delivery.\n- Host-backed `fn` tools are marked `hasFn` in the component manifest (a\n  declared divergence from the reference's all-data posture for\n  orchestrators); user-authored tools are data-only and validated."}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"fe0e4f","exit_code":0,"signal":null}}}}}
