{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"It seems the GreyAvatar parity manifest has some discrepancies. While Meridian .003 implements imitation mark, GreyAvatar lacks it. Also, .003's connector count is significantly lower than GreyAvatar's, and its ethics gate is deeper. Several GreyAvatar-only capabilities like fleet install/deploy, exchange media, and LAN mirror/viewer are absent in .003. The Piper/Edge TTS and whisper STT capabilities are only partially matched by .003's SAPI and WebSpeech implementations."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:37:04.203736900+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm noting that the portrait runner uses procedural SVG, which is functionally equivalent to persona art but uses a different mechanism. The desktop shell is absent, relying on the browser surface, which was a recorded challenge. I have 5 connectors available, with 4 verified plus the local inbox, totaling 5, compared to Grey's approximately 14. For proactive attention, the steward has proactive duties, and Meridian has a temporal-attention duty presented through its persona, indicating partial parity. Spoken input depth is limited to browser WebSpeech, lacking whisper, VAD, or wakeword capabilities. I need to check the Cycle-2 JEV output for existing features and scenario scores to calibrate these findings."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:37:05.557504700+00:00"}}}}
