{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nCycle-2 scored 0.85, but the criteria for counting fleet and exchange media against completeness were added after that cycle. Under the current criteria, these areas are zero, potentially lowering the score. However, the prompt itself states these are optional, so their \"required\" weight is minimal. Despite this, owner ruling dictates they count against completeness. The .003 cycle did address required gaps like temporal reasoning and autonomous work, but the score remains 0.85 due to the fleet/exchange weighting offsetting new channel coverage."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:37:37.408619600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm scoring `time-to-gate` at 3.649 seconds, based on the `msToGate` metric from runtime evidence. Although the convention mentions \"session start to gate pass,\" the evidence clearly indicates this duration is measured from boot start, which I'll report as the basis for the score. The `time to implement` metric is noted as tracked but unscored, with a duration of approximately 29 minutes for this segment."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:37:39.646523600+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'm seeing strong enactment scores across several canonical tasks, particularly for `list-project` (0.95) and `background-present` (0.85). However, `competing-tools` is lower at 0.7, indicating a potential weakness in how I'm comparing or integrating external tools, especially since one is unconfigured. The `restart-recovery` score of 0.9 is good, showing resilience. The `chat-invocation` and `focused-need` tasks also score well at 0.85, suggesting progress in conversational abilities."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:37:42.343237500+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe personality roster has duplicate entries, which I've flagged. Portrait binding is complete, but the \"portrait quality\" is procedural SVG, which might not meet user expectations. The status bar, color schemes, email commentary, context display, and personality editor are all well-enacted. However, the conversation reset doesn't clearly demonstrate its detection of topic shifts, though it does clear the conversation as intended. Launching on Windows via `launch.cmd` is functional but not a true packaged installer, hence the lower score."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:37:45.460171200+00:00"}}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"harsh-church","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe scenario suite score is approximately 0.85, derived from a mean of 24 criteria. Overall, the mean of scored criteria is about 0.61, an improvement from the previous cycle's 0.46, with notable scores in clean launch (0.95) and time-to-gate (1.0), but lower scores in existing features (0.6) and fleet/exchange (0)."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-22T08:37:48.983478600+00:00"}}}}
